meta {
  name: config — anonymous probe reaches the function
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{supabase_url}}/functions/v1/config
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 400
  res.body.error: eq missing_apiKey
}

docs {
  The single most important assertion in this collection.

  400 `missing_apiKey` proves the request REACHED the function and its own guard answered. A 401
  with a `"code":"UNAUTHORIZED_*"` envelope would mean the Supabase gateway rejected it BEFORE the
  function ran — which is precisely the outage that took the paywall down on 2026-09-22 while CI
  smoke stayed green, because that check treated 401 as healthy for every function.

  `config` is a PUBLIC endpoint authenticated by the caller's publishable key, so it must carry
  `verify_jwt = false` in supabase/config.toml. If this assertion ever flips to 401, that block was
  lost and every SDK client is offline.
}
